c. Soldiers are encouraged to attend PME and NCOPDS courses. Achieving distinction while attending PME and NCOPDS courses differentiates Soldiers from their peers.
d. SGTs are encouraged to work towards a college degree or professional credentialing/certifications. Education is an important factor enhancing potential value to the Army and is viewed as an indicator of individual initiative rather than a prerequisite for selection as most/highly qualified. Education is used as a metric to set Soldiers apart from their peers, but it is not a requirement for promotion..
e. Seeking opportunities to learn and succeed is encouraged. These include competing in NCO-of-the-Month Boards, earning the ESB, volunteering for duties/details, and completing correspondence courses.', 'def676879c9c29c4d7cdc035f5b9c0c45cbd8a35aed13850d122ea574a5fc94f', 2, 2, null, 31, null, null, false, null),
