  ('18c90406-10b3-56bc-87e2-381bd72c0725', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35L', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'SSG - CI Sergeant (SL3) — Military Training/Education by Domain', 'Chapter 8. MOS 35L, Counterintelligence (CI) Agent', 'Courses listed here are not all encompassing but illustrate a snapshot of opportunities that can be pursued to add depth and breadth to the knowledge and skills of the SL3 Soldier. Seeking additional training and education, beyond what is listed here, is highly recommended and will differentiate Soldiers from their peers. It is recommended that Soldiers refer to Chapter 3 of this document, the Foundry Course Catalog, the COOL/ArmyIgnitED website, and the ACT website, at a minimum, for developmental opportunities.
(1) Institutional (*When AGR can attend based on assignment): • ALC • Battle Staff Course* • Foundry Training • JCITA Courses* • DCITA Courses* • Antiterrorism Force Protection Level II Course • EJPME I • Operation Security Certification • CI Investigations in a Cyber Environment Course • Cyber Insider Threat Analyst Course • JCHATC* • EOL Course • Ranger School* • Basic Airborne Course* • Jumpmaster Course* • Air Assault School* • SMU OTC
(2) Operational: • JQS/R • STT • ATN - Training and Evaluation Outlines for Individual/Collective/Common Tasks • MOS STP Operational Critical Tasks • MITS • NCOPD
(3) Self-Development. Seeking continuous development in this domain, immaterial of concentration/major and within ones’ own personal and professional interests, is strongly encouraged to bridge gaps between the other education/training domains.', '64324e1810b062fb74545c77a58a197c4d075ca3f45f049cc533c42dc983fb8d', 19, 20, null, 110, null, null, false, null),
  ('41b32827-bc1c-5f64-b036-ec3ec63d6925', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35L', null, 'skills', 'E-7', null, 'SFC - Senior CI Sergeant (SL4) — Skills', 'Chapter 8. MOS 35L, Counterintelligence (CI) Agent', 'In addition to performing duties in the preceding skill level, the Senior CI Sergeant executes and manages missions while leading NCOs, who in-turn lead Soldiers. They are responsible for the evaluation of CI training and provide guidance on the development of the training plan in support of the units’ collective tasks, METL, and the commander’s intent. They review CI related reports and plans and assist in writing, editing, and submitting requests for special investigative techniques and special operational concepts. They build relationships and continuously communicate with leaders in other disciplines and sections to create synergy of effort to maximize effectiveness of the IWfF. The Senior CI Sergeant performs CI Coordinating Authority (CICA) and 2X staff management for subordinate CI elements. They provide technical control and oversight while conducting source and operational management.', '9b810c3243d4fbcf92ae4577f39d5f02682eb401bbdb4f17596d59082867137d', 20, 20, null, 111, null, null, false, null),
  ('97e86016-e5b0-5f0f-ab0c-e0214fb6755f', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'SFC - Senior CI Sergeant (SL4) — KD Assignments', 'Chapter 8. MOS 35L, Counterintelligence (CI) Agent', '• Platoon Sergeant • NCOIC • Detachment Sergeant • SEA/SEL', '3704f3b110e5c1981589e510a05c75f3536108a847730ad4c617dabf0b0bd97d', 20, 20, null, 112, null, null, false, null),
  ('c992fcdc-2bb4-5e1d-915d-2d60ecdb1428', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'SFC - Senior CI Sergeant (SL4) — Operating Assignments', 'Chapter 8. MOS 35L, Counterintelligence (CI) Agent', '• Senior CI Sergeant', '8dd75c28cc015aba36c7161c44eaedc580b7efacada85c6a9622202e39a83365', 20, 20, null, 113, null, null, false, null),
  ('1b48eee7-19eb-5382-802b-1f8228f4f8c7', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'SFC - Senior CI Sergeant (SL4) — Broadening Assignments (*When available to AGR)', 'Chapter 8. MOS 35L, Counterintelligence (CI) Agent', '• Senior Drill Sergeant* • Recruiter* • Senior Instructor/SGL • Career Management NCO* • Talent Management NCO* • OC/T* • Training Developer • Defense Attaché', 'd8e79f023d3d7557188ee89f3382f2fcdcd65870c00911230de6f9550bf766ac', 20, 21, null, 114, null, null, false, null),
  ('c66c39c6-6d9b-50c3-ac78-3325d4cd0476', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35L', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'SFC - Senior CI Sergeant (SL4) — Military Training/Education by Domain', 'Chapter 8. MOS 35L, Counterintelligence (CI) Agent', 'Courses listed here are not all encompassing but illustrate a snapshot of opportunities that can be pursued to add depth and breadth to the knowledge and skills of the SL4 Soldier. Seeking additional training and education, beyond what is listed here, is highly recommended and will differentiate Soldiers from their peers. It is recommended that Soldiers refer to Chapter 3 of this document, the Foundry Course Catalog, the COOL/ArmyIgnitED website, and the ACT website, at a minimum, for developmental opportunities.
(1) Institutional (*When AGR can attend based on assignment): • SLC • Battle Staff Course* • Foundry Training • JCITA Courses* • DCITA Courses* • EJPME II • Operation Security Certification • • JCHATC* • 2X Management Course* • Cyber Insider Threat Analyst Course • EOA Course • Ranger School* • Basic Airborne Course* • Jumpmaster Course* • Air Assault School* • SMU OTC
