  ('cb845877-e996-5035-b6cd-1e9f7de1d91d', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35N', null, 'skills', 'E-7', null, 'SFC – Senior SIGINT Sergeant (SL4) — Skills', 'Chapter 12. MOS 35N, Signals Intelligence (SIGINT) Analyst', 'In addition to performing duties in the preceding skill level, the Senior SIGINT Sergeant executes and manages missions while leading subordinate NCOs. They are responsible for the evaluation of SIGINT training and provide guidance on the development of the training plan in support of the units’ collective tasks, METL, and the commander’s intent. They coordinate the process for SIGINT collection of information with higher, adjacent, and subordinate units to address PIRs and intelligence gaps. They build relationships and continuously communicate with leaders in other disciplines and sections to create synergy of effort to maximize effectiveness of the IWfF. They generate a SIGINT operational readiness strategy and administer the CRITIC testing and evaluation program.', 'a47eecfb527ffd5d7cd719601c459ce3a02a120521100a1ce17b317a4fea5791', 32, 32, null, 153, null, null, false, null),
  ('eb556977-bda6-5594-8dd3-ae1b40e8124d', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35N', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'SFC – Senior SIGINT Sergeant (SL4) — KD Assignments', 'Chapter 12. MOS 35N, Signals Intelligence (SIGINT) Analyst', '• Platoon Sergeant • SEA/SEL • Detachment Sergeant • NCOIC', 'ef12ef4db2f3d3321151f59571f607db69034f22424535448707472ca1370b77', 32, 32, null, 154, null, null, false, null),
  ('f671b3da-e19d-5510-8fa0-e08977286106', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35N', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'SFC – Senior SIGINT Sergeant (SL4) — Operating Assignments', 'Chapter 12. MOS 35N, Signals Intelligence (SIGINT) Analyst', '• Senior SIGINT AnalystOperations Sergeant', 'e6473f82f077d1e0000843ebcbcdc33ea4f0b0f71c535a6709e697c6603fc6a7', 32, 32, null, 155, null, null, false, null),
  ('dc1beec9-076a-5cba-850b-9a9faca78db4', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35N', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'SFC – Senior SIGINT Sergeant (SL4) — Broadening Assignments (*When available to AGR)', 'Chapter 12. MOS 35N, Signals Intelligence (SIGINT) Analyst', '• Senior Drill Sergeant* • Senior Instructor/SGL • Recruiter • Career Management NCO* • Talent Management NCO* • OC/T* • Training Developer* • Capability Developer* • IG NCO • EOA • Defense Attaché*', 'dd7d00ce4c403b510daffa84469dc2276a7809191791561a593f720af1b8d00d', 32, 32, null, 156, null, null, false, null),
  ('f6e3be1b-594a-5674-b2cf-ad11a8e80ec5', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35N', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'SFC – Senior SIGINT Sergeant (SL4) — Military Training/Education by Domain', 'Chapter 12. MOS 35N, Signals Intelligence (SIGINT) Analyst', 'Courses listed here are not all encompassing but illustrate a snapshot of opportunities that can be pursued to add depth and breadth to the knowledge and skills of the SL4 Soldier. Seeking additional training and education, beyond what is listed here, is highly recommended and will differentiate Soldiers from their peers. It is recommended that Soldiers refer to Chapter 3 of this document, the Foundry Course Catalog, the COOL/ArmyIgnitED website, and the ACT website, at a minimum, for developmental opportunities.
(1) Institutional (*When AGR can attend based on assignment): • SLC • Foundry Training • EJPME II • EOA Course • Ranger School* • Basic Airborne Course* • Jumpmaster Course* • Air Assault School* • Battle Staff Course* • SMU OTC
(2) Operational: • JQS/R • STT • ATN - Training and Evaluation Outlines for Individual/Collective/Common Tasks • MOS STP Operational Critical Tasks • MITS • NCOPD
(3) Self-Development. Seeking continuous development in this domain, immaterial of concentration/major and within ones’ own personal and professional interests, is strongly encouraged to bridge gaps between the other education/training domains.', '53a08577e3e12a4b4032ef5fd0d24b661d949d3b9c7e6a45a392bd62941129de', 32, 33, null, 157, null, null, false, null),
  ('dbeafdd6-c23c-555d-bd64-2cc6fdd8d836', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'Soldiers should always strive to exceed the standard regardless of the position currently held. Soldiers must enhance their professionalism by ever-increasing civilian and military education levels and displaying a trend of outstanding quantifiable performance and potential in all positions held when considered against the whole Soldier concept. Soldiers in MOS 35P are encouraged to demonstrate their capabilities and potential by striving to exceed standards in technical proficiency and leadership. It is encouraged that 35P Soldiers seek diversity of duty positions, when possible, to challenge, develop, and illustrate their knowledge and skills. SIGINT Voice Interceptors are encouraged to pursue diverse positions across FORSCOM, INSCOM, TRADOC, and Special Operations/Missions to expand their professional growth and broaden their career development. Proponent Note: Guidance should not be construed as a checklist for promotion selection. It does not guarantee promotion or a competitive Order of Merit number following Evaluation Boards. NCOs who have completed a diverse set of career assignments and have consistently outperformed their peers receiving exceptional rater and senior rater comments are viewed more favorably by board members.', '5510a1bd9e04218c3252304e1be8cb5e41014c016461fd29b1f79b1d1b53af11', 33, 34, null, 158, null, null, false, null),
  ('fe1ed68b-d11a-5cb7-9bff-1b018c3de143', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'skills', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'PVT – SPC/CPL - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL1) — Skills', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'SL1 SIGINT Voice Interceptors collect, analyze, process, exploit, and disseminate information collected via organic SIGINT collection and exploitation equipment, or through access to extended SIGINT enterprise databases. They translate text and voice-based target language material and perform initial analysis of target communications. SIGINT Voice Interceptors use organic collection assets or may be required to construct field crafted collection antennas for collection purposes. They identify target communications signals of interest through target language recognition, extract communications details that meet targeting criteria, and must identify information that meets time-sensitive reporting and CRITIC criteria – all while complying with the SIGINT oversight and compliance programs. They are familiar with their systems and the unit PIR/SIRs to support the IWfF. SIGINT Voice Interceptors must also remain in compliance with AR 11-6 (The Army Language Program).', '0b83b198057333cc6f870832f500968c0dc017102f3fcf4d7bf0652490bb425f', 34, 34, null, 159, null, null, false, null),
  ('63c8188e-9cf8-584e-a5bd-24c02fecdac7', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'PVT – SPC/CPL - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL1) — KD Assignments', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'CPLs can serve in NCOIC positions.', 'c862bb5cd2398283002d3e3b70c34a5ed0ef701ca55a48659fc051d25b4f6748', 34, 34, null, 160, null, null, false, null),
  ('6cde0678-6b1a-503a-9bad-76045211bfaf', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'PVT – SPC/CPL - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL1) — Operating Assignments', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'Primary assignments should focus on building a strong base of technical expertise, basic MOS skills, and common Soldier tasks during the early years of their career. Assignments such as SIGINT Voice Interceptor or Cryptologic Linguist may enhance technical expertise based on various mission sets and laying foundation of tactical knowledge. Soldiers should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility when provided the opportunity.', '314718fbe85c4f8ad0e8bf98dcc53fd0e2744491ab68787549bd8cac9c86ced5', 34, 34, null, 161, null, null, false, null),
  ('4721ed9e-2f0d-521b-9986-3e1ee2b19e1a', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'PVT – SPC/CPL - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL1) — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'There are no broadening assignments for SL1.', 'd9e5aa2b344ecf8cea841e022438b5f716e9716ab37b555fd54b3ff15b82a944', 34, 34, null, 162, null, null, false, null),
  ('d7295014-6415-5e7b-8a46-8033c675b380', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'PVT – SPC/CPL - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL1) — Military Training/Education by Domain', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'Courses listed here are not all encompassing but illustrate a snapshot of opportunities that can be pursued to add depth and breadth to the knowledge and skills of the SL1 Soldier. Seeking additional training and education, beyond what is listed here, is highly recommended and will differentiate Soldiers from their peers. It is recommended that Soldiers refer to Chapter 3 of this document, the Foundry Course Catalog, the COOL/ArmyIgnitED website, and the ACT website, at a minimum, for developmental opportunities.
(1) Institutional (*When AGR can attend based on assignment): • Foundry Training • NSA Internship Programs • Basic, Intermediate, and Advanced DLIFLC Courses • APG Operator Course* • Ranger School* • Basic Airborne Course* • Air Assault School*
(2) Operational: • JQS/R • STT • ATN - Training and Evaluation Outlines for Individual/Collective/Common Tasks • MOS STP Operational Critical Tasks • MITS • NCOPD
(3) Self-Development. Seeking continuous development in this domain, immaterial of concentration/major and within ones’ own personal and professional interests, is strongly encouraged to bridge gaps between the other education/training domains.', 'c408b6ca3aefac727a6539f6d5c7ba14f962ffaea675788f519bef6e9dcfab45', 34, 34, null, 163, null, null, false, null),
  ('b25493f1-004a-53cf-911a-4dbf468b740b', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'skills', 'E-5', null, 'SGT - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL2) — Skills', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', 'In addition to mastering duties in the preceding skill level, the SL2 SIGINT Voice Interceptor trains and leads subordinate Soldiers. They execute daily SIGINT operations related to the processing, and exploitation of foreign communications whether collected by organic assets, or accessed over extended SIGNT enterprise databases, and enable SIGINT support to the targeting process. When operating organic collection systems, they must survey and establish the collection sites to be used by the collection teams. They are responsible for planning and directing access to SIGINT systems while reporting the status of those systems to higher echelons. They are responsible for maintaining the language training plans for their subordinates. SL2 SIGINT Voice Interceptors enforce the standards for oversight and compliance programs, audit the use of SIGINT databases, and validate SIGINT reporting. They are directly responsible for the team and equipment associated with SIGINT training and collection missions.', '88ade907800c3f7c5fae406e245bc8281f846060049c2fab8915ea8b6c0a1d5a', 35, 35, null, 164, null, null, false, null),
  ('c093bca9-627c-5aff-8798-37d86962ba39', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'SGT - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL2) — KD Assignments', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', '• Team Leader • NCOIC', 'c3f902e5dc690df89be48bf73a721cab216caf05fa1bfd557b9a2a65df2e9848', 35, 35, null, 165, null, null, false, null),
  ('e6e6ec62-b920-597c-bbcf-f22f498ed249', '1396060f-5555-5ed7-a918-43972de6ad68', 'Army', 'enlisted', '35P', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'SGT - SIGINT Voice Interceptor (SL2) — Operating Assignments', 'Chapter 14. MOS 35P, SIGINT Voice Interceptor', '• SIGINT Voice Interceptor • Cryptologic Linquist • Special Operations Team-Alpha (SOT-A) Team Member', '9914094679c6279f70b6d7049d77fcb325b58b5ac7cba941113ba0be86d6c3a9', 35, 35, null, 166, null, null, false, null),
